    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "An Appeal for Israel’s Repentance"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "label",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "To the Chief Musician. On an instrument of Gath. A Psalm of Asaph."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Sing aloud to God our strength;",
          "Make a joyful shout to the God of Jacob."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Raise a song and strike the timbrel,",
          "The pleasant harp with the lute."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Blow the trumpet at the time of the New Moon,",
          "At the full moon, on our solemn feast day."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For this is a statute for Israel,",
          "A law of the God of Jacob."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "This He established in Joseph as a testimony,",
          "When He went throughout the land of Egypt,",
          "Where I heard a language I did not understand."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“I removed his shoulder from the burden;",
          "His hands were freed from the baskets."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "You called in trouble, and I delivered you;",
          "I answered you in the secret place of thunder;",
          "I tested you at the waters of Meribah."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "label",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Selah"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          8
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“Hear, O My people, and I will admonish you!",
          "O Israel, if you will listen to Me!"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "There shall be no foreign god among you;",
          "Nor shall you worship any foreign god."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          10
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I am the Lord your God,",
          "Who brought you out of the land of Egypt;",
          "Open your mouth wide, and I will fill it."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          11
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“But My people would not heed My voice,",
          "And Israel would have none of Me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          12
        ],
        "lines": [
          "So I gave them over to their own stubborn heart,",
          "To walk in their own counsels."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          13
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“Oh, that My people would listen to Me,",
          "That Israel would walk in My ways!"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          14
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I would soon subdue their enemies,",
          "And turn My hand against their adversaries."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          15
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The haters of the Lord would pretend submission to Him,",
          "But their fate would endure forever."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          16
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He would have fed them also with the finest of wheat;",
          "And with honey from the rock I would have satisfied you.”"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      }
    ]
  },
